# Ford Granada Mk III five-door hatchback, 1985-1994.
#
# The last Granada: the aerodynamic five-door hatchback (the saloon and
# estate are 4.744 m), with the low grille and body-coloured bumpers. Renamed
# Scorpio in 1994. The hatchback the pack photographs is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Granada_(Europe)
#
# Dimensions 4.673 x 1.760 x 1.440 m, wheelbase 2.761 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a rear
# three-quarter about 30 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no 1985-94 chart was obtained. The 1981 Ford colour and
# trim guide is a lead for the outgoing Mk II, not evidence for the Mk III.
# Diamond White, Midnight Blue, Venetian Red and Strato Silver are plain
# names used with that caveat. Weights 30, 30, 25, 25, total 110,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90: the largest
# executive Ford of its day. Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1985 intro, retires staggered 2010-2013.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-granada-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-granada-mk3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-granada-mk3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: image 1 is front-oblique, not rear-oblique as labelled,
# and there is no true side elevation. The hatch glass and lamp corners are too
# angular, and the bumper rubbing strip is simplified. At 128 px the sloping
# five-door hatch, low grille and wraparound lamps read as a Granada Mk III.


